# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "The signer transcript: what was asked, shown and approved"
description: """
Binds the bytes a signature will cover to the meaning a human was shown and
to the policy that approved it, under one versioned envelope.

The binding is structural rather than procedural. The intent is derived from
the payload bytes and the rendering is derived from the intent, so a signer
that displayed one transaction and signed another is not something this API
can express -- and an approval cannot be constructed without a review, nor a
review without the policy having passed.

No clock: freshness is checked against a time the caller supplies. A signer
able to read a clock could be walked into extending its own validity window."""
